+---
+title: "Puter"
+description: "Use Puter models with Docker Agent by signing in with a Puter account instead of buying provider API keys."
+keywords: docker agent, ai agents, model providers, llm, puter, openai-compatible, sign in
+linkTitle: "Puter"
+weight: 285
+---
+
+_Use Puter models with Docker Agent by signing in with a Puter account instead of buying provider API keys._
+
+## Overview
+
+[Puter](https://puter.com) exposes an **OpenAI-compatible endpoint** that serves models from many vendors
+(GPT, Claude, Gemini, Grok, DeepSeek, Qwen, GLM, Kimi, …) authenticated with a **Puter account token**
+instead of per-vendor API keys.
+
+Docker Agent connects to it as a normal OpenAI-compatible provider, so you only need:
+
+1. A Puter account (free tier available; usage is billed to your own Puter account — the
+   ["user-pays" model](https://docs.puter.com/user-pays-model/)).
+2. A Puter auth token — either from <https://puter.com/dashboard> or by signing in with the helper in
+   [`puter/`](https://github.com/docker/docker-agent/tree/main/puter).
+
+## Configuration
+
+```yaml
+providers:
+  puter:
+    provider: openai
+    api_type: openai_chatcompletions # required, see note below
+    base_url: https://api.puter.com/puterai/openai/v1/
+    token_key: PUTER_AUTH_TOKEN
+
+models:
+  puter_fast:
+    provider: puter
+    model: gpt-5.4-nano
+    max_tokens: 8192
+
+agents:
+  root:
+    model: puter_fast
+    instruction: You are a helpful assistant.
+```
+
+```sh
+export PUTER_AUTH_TOKEN=...        # or use --env-from-file
+docker agent run examples/puter.yaml
+```
+
+> [!IMPORTANT]
+> **Always set `api_type: openai_chatcompletions`**
+>
+> Puter only serves the legacy Chat Completions API. Without an explicit `api_type`, Docker Agent picks
+> the API from the model name (e.g. `gpt-5.x`, o-series and Codex default to `openai_responses`),
+> which Puter rejects.
+
+## Signing in with the helper
+
+The [`puter/`](https://github.com/docker/docker-agent/tree/main/puter) directory in this repository contains
+a small Node helper that performs a browser sign-in, stores the token in `puter/.env.puter` (mode `600`) and
+can verify the account:
+
+```sh
+npm install --prefix puter
+node puter/puter-login.mjs          # browser sign-in → puter/.env.puter
+node puter/puter-login.mjs --verify # check the token and show the account
+./puter/run-agent.sh "hello"        # run Docker Agent with the stored token
+```
+
+On machines without a browser (SSH, containers) copy the printed login URL to your own browser, or create a
+token on the Puter dashboard and store it with `node puter/puter-login.mjs --set-token <token>`.
+
+## Notes
+
+- **Tool calling** requires a model that supports function calling — use the GPT/Claude/Gemini families for
+  agentic work.
+- **Quota** is yours: `docker agent` calls are billed to the Puter account behind the token. Check usage with
+  `node puter/puter-login.mjs --verify` or on the Puter dashboard.
+- **Model names** are Puter's: `gpt-5.4-nano`, `claude-sonnet-5`, `gemini-3.1-flash-lite`, `grok-4-1-fast`,
+  `openai/gpt-oss-120b`, `deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash`, …
+
+## Reference
+
+- Puter — OpenAI-compatible endpoint: <https://developer.puter.com/tutorials/use-openai-sdk-with-puter/>
+- Puter — Node.js sign-in: <https://developer.puter.com/tutorials/puter-js-node-js/>
+- Example config: [`examples/puter.yaml`](https://github.com/docker/docker-agent/blob/main/examples/puter.yaml)
